# RESEARCH & TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE: OILTRACE / MARITIME FORENSICS PIPELINE

This document synthesizes the core data repositories, simulation frameworks, AIS tracking APIs, and open-source models required for satellite-based oil spill detection, reverse Lagrangian backtracking, and candidate vessel attribution.

---

## 1. Deep Learning & Satellite Imagery Datasets

### **Sentinel-1 SAR Oil Spill Image Datasets (Parts I & III)**
* **Zenodo Links:**
  * [Part I Repository (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.8346860)](https://zenodo.org/records/8346860)
  * [Part III Repository (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.13761290)](https://zenodo.org/records/13761290)
* **Authors:** Trujillo-Acatitla, R., Tuxpan-Vargas, J., Ovando-Vázquez, C., & Monterrubio-Martínez, E. (2024).
* **Contents & Format:** 
  * Consists of large-scale Sentinel-1 Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) imagery collections designed for training, validating, and testing deep learning segmentation architectures.
  * Provides Sigma0 ($\sigma^0$) images in decibels ($\text{dB}$) across dual polarizations (**VV** and **VH**).
  * Includes corresponding binary pixel-level segmentation masks separating true oil slicks from look-alikes (e.g., biogenic slicks, low-wind areas, algal blooms).
* **Integration Strategy:** Used to train backbone segmentation models (e.g., U-Net, SegFormer) to extract accurate spatial polygons of oil slicks from raw C-band satellite imagery.

### **Companion Processing Toolkit: `slicksmith_ttom`**
* **PyPI Reference:** [slicksmith_ttom on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/slicksmith_ttom/)
* **Functionality:** Provides specialized Python preprocessing routines for organizing Zenodo SAR datasets, structuring raster files for **TorchGeo** compatibility, adding pseudo-timestamps, and georeferencing raster label TIFFs to enable seamless intersection sampling.

