## 3. Lagrangian Drift Simulation & Backtracking

### **OpenDrift / OpenOil Framework**
* **GitHub Repository:** [OpenDrift/opendrift](https://github.com/OpenDrift/opendrift)
* **Architecture:** Python-based framework for trajectory and drift modeling of objects and substances in the ocean. 
* **Core Mechanics for OilTrace:**
  * **Forward Drift (Forecasting):** Simulates weathering, evaporation, dispersion, and movement of oil particles under wind and current forces.
  * **Backward Drift (Hindcasting / Backtracking):** Reverses time steps using historical ERA5 wind fields and CMEMS ocean currents to trace an observed slick polygon back to its geographic **Source Corridor ($S$)** and **Origin Time Window ($T$)**.
* **Integration Strategy:** Implemented as the physics core in Python to compute probabilistic origin heatmaps instead of relying on static proximity radius calculations.

