## 4. Vessel Traffic & AIS Data Integration

### **MarineCadastre AIS Data**
* **Portal Link:** [marinecadastre.gov/accessais](https://marinecadastre.gov/accessais/)
* **Contents:** Historical Automatic Identification System (AIS) vessel tracking data, including timestamped positions, Maritime Mobile Service Identities (MMSI), Speed Over Ground (SOG), Course Over Ground (COG), and vessel metadata.
* **Role in Pipeline:** Used to reconstruct vessel tracks passing through or near reconstructed source corridors during the estimated release window.

### **Global Fishing Watch (GFW): Radar-Illuminated Ocean**
* **Data Portal:** [globalfishingwatch.org/data/radar-illuminated-ocean](https://globalfishingwatch.org/data/radar-illuminated-ocean/)
* **Contents:** Datasets combining satellite radar observations with vessel tracking data to uncover dark targets—vessels operating with their AIS transponders turned off or obstructed.
* **Role in Pipeline:** Informs the **Incomplete-AIS & Gap Reasoning** module, helping distinguish between routine satellite coverage blackouts and intentional transponder disablement near spill sites.

